---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import fs from 'node:fs';
import path from 'node:path';

const photoPath = path.join(process.cwd(), 'public', 'brian-photo-ref.jpg');
const hasPhoto = fs.existsSync(photoPath);
---
<BaseLayout
  title="About — Brian Beers"
  description="Operator and investor helping owners buy, grow, and scale proven business models — based on real ops, not theory."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="grid items-start gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[1.1fr_0.9fr] lg:gap-14">
      <div>
        <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-navy sm:text-5xl">Hi, I’m Brian</h1>
        <p class="mt-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-navy/75">
          I’m an operator, investor, and multi-unit franchisee. For more than a decade I’ve built a portfolio of
          businesses that today generate $50M+ in revenue a year — starting with two underperforming locations and
          a simple focus: people, performance, and profit.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-navy/70">
          My mission is straightforward: help owners earn more cash flow, grow with confidence, and build something
          they’re proud of. Everything I share comes from real operating experience — not theory, not hype, and not
          what looks good on a pitch deck.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-navy/70">
          I didn’t invent software or raise venture capital. I followed proven systems, outworked the competition,
          and learned to lead strong teams. That’s the real cheat code: pick a model that works, then execute.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="flex justify-center lg:justify-end">
        {hasPhoto ? (
          <img
            src="/brian-photo-ref.jpg"
            alt="Brian Beers"
            class="h-72 w-72 rounded-3xl object-cover shadow-lg ring-1 ring-border sm:h-80 sm:w-80"
            width="320"
            height="320"
          />
        ) : (
          <div class="flex h-72 w-72 items-center justify-center rounded-3xl bg-navy/5 text-navy/40 ring-1 ring-border sm:h-80 sm:w-80">
            Photo coming soon
          </div>
        )}
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-14 grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-3">
      <div class="card">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-navy">Real ops</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-navy/70">
          Playbooks from turning around shops and scaling multi-unit — not classroom theory.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-navy">Proven systems</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-navy/70">
          Franchise operator credibility applied to brand-agnostic models: buy right, run tight, grow with intent.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-navy">Soft next steps</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-navy/70">
          Free guides and a conversation when you’re ready. No pitch-deck dump, no earnings promises.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-16 max-w-3xl">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-navy sm:text-3xl">The journey</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-navy/70">
        I started in auto repair. In 2016, my brother Chris and I bought two existing shops. Those locations became
        the seed of a bigger operating portfolio.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-navy/70">
        From 2017 to 2019 we added more locations. After COVID, we acquired a seven-store group that opened a new
        market. By the end of 2021 we were at 21 Midas locations. We kept buying through 2022–2025.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-navy/70">
        Today we operate 35 Midas Auto Repair franchises across Philadelphia and New Jersey. I’m also an
        investor and partner in other brands — Waterloo Turf, Senior Care, B2B Kitchen Services, and Home Services.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-navy/70">
        The through-line isn’t a single brand. It’s owning the outcome: buying the right vehicle, fixing what
        underperforms, and building systems that scale.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-16 max-w-3xl">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-navy sm:text-3xl">How I can help</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-navy/70">
        Different starting points. Same goal: more cash flow, more confidence, and a clearer path.
      </p>

      <div class="mt-8 space-y-6">
        <div class="rounded-2xl border border-border bg-white p-6 shadow-sm">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-navy">Buying or entering ownership</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-navy/70">
            If you’re exploring your first acquisition or franchise, I help you avoid common traps, compare
            models honestly, and understand the real economics before you commit. Start with the
            <a href="/buy" class="font-semibold text-navy underline decoration-accent/60 underline-offset-2 hover:text-accent">Buy</a>
            door and the free guides on this site.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-2xl border border-border bg-white p-6 shadow-sm">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-navy">Existing owners who want to scale</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-navy/70">
            If you already own and want better profit, stronger managers, or your next location, I share the same
            operating habits used to grow from 2 to 35 units — tighten the unit, build leadership layers, and
            structure acquisitions without burning out. Explore
            <a href="/grow" class="font-semibold text-navy underline decoration-accent/60 underline-offset-2 hover:text-accent">Grow</a>,
            or <a href="/contact" class="font-semibold text-navy underline decoration-accent/60 underline-offset-2 hover:text-accent">reach out</a>
            when you want to talk it through.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-2xl border border-border bg-white p-6 shadow-sm">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-navy">Here to learn</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-navy/70">
            Free, practical content on buying the right vehicle, turning around underperformers, and scaling
            multi-unit — franchisee-first experience applied to proven business models. Grab
            <a href="/contact?intent=guide" class="font-semibold text-navy underline decoration-accent/60 underline-offset-2 hover:text-accent">The Copy-Paste Millionaire</a>
            guide when you’re ready.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-16 max-w-3xl">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-navy sm:text-3xl">Lessons learned</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-navy/70">
        I’ve chased shiny objects — new tactics inside the business, side ventures outside it. Every time I
        drifted, growth slowed. Every time I returned to fundamentals, things took off.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-navy/70">
        The biggest lesson is simple: focus on less, then obsess. Pick the few levers that actually move profit,
        and go all in on them. That’s how you build something durable.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-14 rounded-2xl border border-border bg-white p-8 text-center shadow-sm sm:p-10">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-navy">Want to talk it through?</h2>
      <p class="mx-auto mt-3 max-w-xl text-navy/65">
        Share where you are — buying, growing, or still figuring out the door — and we’ll go from there. Or
        download the free guide on how ordinary people build extraordinary businesses by scaling proven models.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-3">
        <a href="/contact" class="btn-primary">Get in touch</a>
        <a href="/contact?intent=guide" class="btn-secondary">Get the free guide</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
